  "aiContextParagraph": "The Samajwadi Party and the Congress are currently engaged in complex negotiations regarding seat-sharing arrangements for the upcoming Uttar Pradesh assembly elections. While reports indicate that the Samajwadi Party has offered Congress 26 seats to begin the alliance process, tensions have surfaced following Congress's request for additional constituencies. The situation escalated recently when the Samajwadi Party unveiled its first list of five candidates, which included two seats that were reportedly part of the Congress party's initial wishlist. In response to the ongoing friction, Samajwadi Party leader Akhilesh Yadav publicly urged his alliance partner to focus on serious discussions and prioritize the collective goal of winning the majority of seats in the state. The negotiation process remains active as both parties navigate their individual political objectives against the challenges of forming a unified front for the polls.",
